 ## 5. Technical Design
 
-### Architecture Layers
+### Repository Pattern Architecture
 
 ```
 HTTP Request
     ↓
-Blueprint Route (routes/tasks.py)
+Blueprint Route (routes/tasks.py)        ← unchanged
     ↓
-TaskService (services/task_service.py)
+TaskService (services/task_service.py)   ← accepts ITaskRepository
     ↓
-TaskStorage (services/task_storage.py)
+ITaskRepository (repositories/base.py)   ← interface contract
     ↓
-tasks.json
+FileTaskRepository  OR  DatabaseTaskRepository
 ```
 
-### API Endpoints (unchanged from Sprint 2)
+### Swappable Backends
 
-| Method | Endpoint | Purpose | Status Codes |
-|--------|----------|---------|--------------|
-| GET | `/api/health` | Health check | 200 |
-| GET | `/api/tasks` | Retrieve all tasks | 200 |
-| POST | `/api/tasks` | Create new task | 201, 400 |
-| PUT | `/api/tasks/<id>` | Mark task complete | 200, 404 |
-| DELETE | `/api/tasks/<id>` | Delete task | 200, 404 |
-
-> No new endpoints in Sprint 3 — architecture changes only.
+```python
+create_app()              → FileTaskRepository()      → tasks.json
+create_app(use_db=True)   → DatabaseTaskRepository()  → tasks.db
+mocker.MagicMock()        → no I/O at all (tests)
+```
 
